import Mathlib

-- This sub-lemma states that the ideal generated by 1 in the integers is the
-- entire ring (the top ideal, `⊤`). Mathlib provides `Ideal.span_singleton_one`
-- for this purpose, which is applicable to any semiring.
lemma ideal_span_one_eq_top : Ideal.span {(1 : ℤ)} = ⊤ := by
  exact Ideal.span_singleton_one

-- This sub-lemma states that for any ring `R`, the quotient by an ideal `I`
-- that is equal to the top ideal `⊤` is isomorphic to the null ring (`PUnit`).
-- The initial proof skeleton suggested using `Ideal.quotTop`, but that requires
-- `CommRing R`. As hinted in the problem description, `Ideal.quotientEquivOfEqTop`
-- is the more general and correct lemma to use here, as it only requires `Ring R`.